    "sources": {
     "budget_mg": "Gliadel label / NICE TA121: at most 8 wafers x 7.7 mg BCNU = 61.6 mg, the clinical maximum (grounding report, delivery ledger). A per-case cap, never scaled by perceived volume and never tuned.",
     "d_star_cm2_s": "Free TMA+ diffusivity 1.311e-5 cm2/s at 37 C (Vorisek & Sykova 1997, J Neurophysiol 78:912) divided by gray-matter tortuosity^2 with lambda ~ 1.55-1.60 (Hrabetova et al. 2018, J Neurosci 38:9355) gives D* ~ 5.1e-6 cm2/s. DECLARED SUBSTITUTION: no measured BCNU effective diffusivity in brain exists; the small-molecule TMA value stands in.",
     "k_clear_s": "Bork et al. 2024, PNAS 121(16):e2318444121: the Groothuis replication of the efflux constant, about 5x faster, = 6.0e-4 /s, a difference the authors attribute to anaesthetic choice. HIGH end of a genuine 5x literature conflict; not rounding, so both ends are carried and every result is reported for both.",
